# MEASURED 2026-07-30, and this is the one that matters most on this board.
# Under memory pressure the kernel kills by oom_score, and birdnet_analysis --
# the bird detector, the entire point of the station -- currently scores 796,
# the HIGHEST of any process on the box (daily_plot 752, caddy 677, ffmpeg 676;
# every oom_score_adj is 0). So an OOM during a 1.6 GB upload on a 990 MB board
# with 302 MB available would reap the DETECTOR first.
#
# systemd MemoryMax= cannot help: /proc/cmdline carries cgroup_disable=memory, so
# the kernel memory controller is off and MemoryAccounting=yes is a false green.
# OOMScoreAdjust is NOT a cgroup feature -- it is a per-process /proc attribute --
# so it still works here (verified: set to 1000, read back 1000).
#
# Pinning the backup to 1000 makes IT the designated victim. That trade is free:
# rclone copy is resumable and deletes nothing, so a killed backup costs one
# retry, while a killed detector costs birdsong that no retry can recover.
OOMScoreAdjust=1000

